  "answer": "**Production usage:** only in the locale root layout.\n\n`GlobalScriptsSDK` is imported and rendered in `app/[locale]/layout.tsx` inside `<head>`, right after `TBAnalyticsStubScript`:\n\n```41:41:app/[locale]/layout.tsx\nimport GlobalScriptsSDK from '../components/GlobalScripts/GlobalScriptsSDK';\n```\n\n```217:227:app/[locale]/layout.tsx\n        <TBAnalyticsStubScript />\n        <NavigationStylesheet logger={context.logger} requestHeaders={context.requestHeaders} />\n        <GlobalScriptsSDK\n          config={{\n            brand,\n            locale,\n            page,\n            runtimeConfig,\n            debug: env.GLOBAL_SCRIPTS_DEBUG,\n          }}\n        />\n```\n\nThat mounts it for every locale-scoped page under that layout.\n\n**Also referenced (not mounted):**\n- **Tests:** `app/components/GlobalScripts/__tests__/GlobalScriptsSDK.test.tsx` — renders the component directly.\n- **Comments only:** `AnalyticsLifecycleTracker.tsx` notes that `GlobalScriptsSDK` owns the initial `page_view`; it does not import or render it.\n\n**Definition:** `app/components/GlobalScripts/GlobalScriptsSDK.tsx` (`export default function GlobalScriptsSDK`).",
